{"id": "q0184", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1695060334, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": -1, "query": "A circular opening of radius 0.8mm in an opaque screen is illuminated by plane waves of monochromatic light and the emergent light allowed to fall on a movable screen. As the screen is gradually brought toward the aperture, it is found that a succession of alternately light and dark spots appear at the center of the diffraction patterns. (a) If a bright spot appears for the second time when the distance from the screen to the position of the screen required for a bright spot to appear for the first time is 36.2 cm, find the wavelength of the light. (b) If a dark spot appears for the second time when the distance between the screen and the position of the screen required for a dark spot to appear for the first time is 36.2 cm, find the wavelength of the light. (c) Find at what distance from the screen to the aperture a bright spot appeared for the first time (refer to part (a)). (d) Find at what distance from the screen to the aperture a dark spot appeared for the first time (refer to part (b)).\n\nA. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.25 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 460mμ, First bright spot: 57 cm, First dark spot: 69 cm\nB. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.17 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 442mμ, First bright spot: 54.7 cm, First dark spot: 72.4 cm\nC. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.5 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 500mμ, First bright spot: 55 cm, First dark spot: 72 cm\nD. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.3 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 450mμ, First bright spot: 56 cm, First dark spot: 70 cm\nE. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.4 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 480mμ, First bright spot: 58 cm, First dark spot: 74 cm\nF. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.0 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 420mμ, First bright spot: 52 cm, First dark spot: 75 cm\nG. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.3 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 465mμ, First bright spot: 56.5 cm, First dark spot: 70.5 cm\nH. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.2 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 440mμ, First bright spot: 54 cm, First dark spot: 73 cm\nI. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.1 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 435mμ, First bright spot: 53 cm, First dark spot: 71 cm\nJ. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.15 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 450mμ, First bright spot: 55.5 cm, First dark spot: 71.5 cm\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0184.wav", "input_sha256": "15e49d4956f4502392d4e2d29350ef7e9e4a2bfe9d47598ab8080f0e14f26247", "input_samples": 2833000, "input_s": 177.062, "n_real_chunks": 178, "score": 0.7601, "act": 0.9988, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Using Fresnel half-period zones for a circular aperture, \\[ r^2 = n\\lambda z \\] where \\(r=0.8\\text{ mm}=8.0\\times10^{-4}\\text{ m}\\), so \\[ r^2=6.4\\times10^{-7}\\text{ m}^2 \\] Bright center occurs for odd \\(n=1,3,5,\\dots\\); dark center occurs for even \\(n=2,4,6,\\dots\\). A. Note especially that \\(460\\ \\mu\\text{m}\\) should likely be \\(0.460\\ \\mu\\text{m}\\) or \\(460\\text{ nm}\\).", "expert_answer": "Using Fresnel half-period zones for a circular aperture,\n\n\\[\nr^2 = n\\lambda z\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(r=0.8\\text{ mm}=8.0\\times10^{-4}\\text{ m}\\), so\n\n\\[\nr^2=6.4\\times10^{-7}\\text{ m}^2\n\\]\n\nBright center occurs for odd \\(n=1,3,5,\\dots\\); dark center occurs for even \\(n=2,4,6,\\dots\\).\n\n## A. Wavelength for bright spots\n\nFirst bright: \\(n=1\\)\n\nSecond bright: \\(n=3\\)\n\n\\[\nz_1=\\frac{r^2}{\\lambda},\\qquad z_2=\\frac{r^2}{3\\lambda}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\n\\[\nz_1-z_2=0.362\\text{ m}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{r^2}{\\lambda}-\\frac{r^2}{3\\lambda}=0.362\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{2r^2}{3\\lambda}=0.362\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\lambda=\\frac{2r^2}{3(0.362)}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\lambda=\\frac{2(6.4\\times10^{-7})}{1.086}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\lambda \\approx 1.18\\times10^{-6}\\text{ m}}\n\\]\n\n## B. Wavelength for dark spots\n\nFirst dark: \\(n=2\\)\n\nSecond dark: \\(n=4\\)\n\n\\[\nz_1=\\frac{r^2}{2\\lambda},\\qquad z_2=\\frac{r^2}{4\\lambda}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nz_1-z_2=0.362\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{r^2}{4\\lambda}=0.362\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\lambda=\\frac{r^2}{4(0.362)}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\lambda=\\frac{6.4\\times10^{-7}}{1.448}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\lambda \\approx 4.42\\times10^{-7}\\text{ m}}\n\\]\n\nor\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0.442\\ \\mu\\text{m}}\n\\]\n\n## C. First bright distance\n\nFrom part A:\n\n\\[\nz_1=\\frac{r^2}{\\lambda}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nz_1=\\frac{6.4\\times10^{-7}}{1.18\\times10^{-6}}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{z_1\\approx 0.543\\text{ m}=54.3\\text{ cm}}\n\\]\n\n## D. First dark distance\n\nFrom part B:\n\n\\[\nz_1=\\frac{r^2}{2\\lambda}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nz_1=\\frac{6.4\\times10^{-7}}{2(4.42\\times10^{-7})}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{z_1\\approx 0.724\\text{ m}=72.4\\text{ cm}}\n\\]\n\nSo the correct results are:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\lambda_{\\text{bright}}\\approx 1.18\\times10^{-6}\\text{ m}}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\lambda_{\\text{dark}}\\approx 4.42\\times10^{-7}\\text{ m}}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{z_{\\text{first bright}}\\approx 54.3\\text{ cm}}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{z_{\\text{first dark}}\\approx 72.4\\text{ cm}}\n\\]\n\nThe provided answer values \\(1.25\\times10^{-6}\\text{ m}\\), \\(460\\ \\mu\\text{m}\\), \\(57\\text{ cm}\\), and \\(69\\text{ cm}\\) are not correct. Note especially that \\(460\\ \\mu\\text{m}\\) should likely be \\(0.460\\ \\mu\\text{m}\\) or \\(460\\text{ nm}\\).", "transcript": "A circular opening of radius 0.8 millimeters in an opaque screen is illuminated by plane waves of monochromatic light, and the emergent light allowed to fall on a movable screen. As the screen is gradually brought toward the aperture, it is found that a succession of alternately light and dark spots", "asr_s": 7.73, "expert_s": 16.93, "expert_input_samples": 1168000, "expert_input_s": 73.0, "expert_input_sha256": "655fc40f20bfe63c84963d167b8094d208da000a618deb5176da711d488038c5", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 16.758, "relay_synth_ms": 56188, "onset_chunk": 72, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 7, "feed_lag_max_ms": 2462, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 11676, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0184_aggressive_relay.wav", "sha256": "69e460a235780f4c5e7696b52af2a2f57b38e11030aab54dcac408036b3bf701", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 145.24}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0184_aggressive_candidate.wav", "sha256": "0928a9a0eee1b36f3f9fc58b762034ff96453dafb90450ab075cc39b9a80afa5", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0184_aggressive_stall.wav", "sha256": "81e84e702851928476f72886bbd6bbcc12e30934c90c36fee8580926c0b27ea6", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 8.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.053, 1.098, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.054, 2.098, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.055, 3.099, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.054, 4.099, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.054, 5.098, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.055, 6.101, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.055, 7.101, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.057, 8.102, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.055, 9.1, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.056, 10.101, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.056, 11.102, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.057, 12.103, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.057, 13.102, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.057, 14.104, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.057, 15.103, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.058, 16.103, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17.0, 17.059, 17.104, 1, 0, 0], [17, 1, 18.0, 18.06, 18.106, 1, 0, 0], [